at that time\". \n\nI see the inflation calculation is more nuanced. The problem wants to convert historical prices to a consistent dollar value, not adjust each price individually. This means taking the nominal silver price and converting it to a standard reference year's dollars using the CPI ratio. The key is finding the appropriate inflation adjustment that reflects purchasing power across different time periods.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_468550217adc485d9eb50625","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"curl -sL \"https://www.usgs.gov/media/files/silver-prices-1940-1960\" 2>&1 | head -30"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
