38/1948, $1.294/oz for 1958)\n\n\n3. Find the \"real\" or inflation-adjusted value by using the actual market price adjusted for inflation to today's dollars\n\nI'll track down the historical silver prices to complete the calculation. Finding reliable data from 1938, 1948, and 1958 will be crucial for an accurate inflation adjustment.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_928008e1cc3c4dd69b3a4124","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request\nimport json\n\n# Try to fetch World Bank data for silver prices\nurl = 'https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/USA/indicator/FP.CPI.TOTL?format=json'\ntry:\n    response = urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=10)\n    data = json.loads(response.read().decode())\n    print(json.dumps(data[:2], indent=2) if data else 'No data')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'Error: {e}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
